id: pm-qswf81
title: "GH-677: pm-path relocation must diagnose extension discovery changes"
description: "GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/677 reports that --pm-path silently relocates extension discovery and extension commands vanish without a targeted diagnostic. Make storage and source discovery coordinates explicit and actionable."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-25T02:06:35.414Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T17:24:18.031Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T17:05:51.959Z"
author: unknown
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Storage root and extension discovery root are surfaced as explicit, separately named coordinates in diagnostics rather than one implied path; When --pm-path relocates discovery so that previously available extension commands are absent, the unknown-command error names the relocation as the probable cause and states the corrective flag; Coverage asserts the diagnostic on a relocated workspace whose extension set differs from the default"
parent: pm-usfg
release: v2026.7.26
resolution: pm-path relocation diagnostics are deterministic across clean and package-populated workspaces.
expected_result: pm-path relocation diagnostics are deterministic across clean and package-populated workspaces.
actual_result: "The CLI compares implicit workspace and selected tracker command surfaces; an initialized two-root acceptance fixture passes on clean runners. Exact-head proof: 25 linked tests, 6,370 repository tests, and 100/100/100/100 coverage."
